      "math_academy_id": "q-1402",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "The vector $u$ has magnitude $13,$ the vector $v$ has magnitude $2,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${96}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to two decimal places where appropriate.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =13\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{96}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =26\\cdot (0.994\\,52…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(25.857\\,56…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈25.86n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
